=== Analysis Class Diagram <sec-a-pay-ac>

@fig-a-pay-ac is the analysis model. The Buyer works through `PaymentUI`; Stripe reaches the system only through the gateway boundary `PaymentGateway`, which both receives Stripe's report (`paid`) and is asked to verify and read it back. `PayUpfrontControl` realises the use case and is the only object that talks to both boundaries and to the entities. `BaseUseCaseControl` is an abstract control, a role: it stands for the control of the including use case, which is `StartTeamControl` in UC3 or `JoinTeamControl` in UC4. Pay upfront calls its one operation, `paymentConfirmed(payment)`, the same name the base use cases use, and does not know what the money buys; in design the role becomes the port `PaymentBusinessPort` (S3). Attributes sit on entities only, in analysis types; `PaymentStatus`, `PaymentOutcome`, `RefundStatus`, `ReviewStatus` and `ReportResult` are enumerations. A payment owes at most one refund and is held by at most one review case. Each Stripe report is a `ProviderReport`, keyed by its event id; recording it is how a repeat is recognised (A11), and because it can exist without a payment it also expresses a report about a payment BlocBuy never held (A10). The refund is a plain association: it has its own lifecycle (@sec-a-uc06).

The entities use the canonical names of the system view (@sec-a-reading). `Payment` and `Refund` are drawn here with every attribute; UC3 and UC4 show the subset they use. `PurchaseIntent` shows only what Pay upfront reads; its full model and its operations, such as `fulfilBy(payment)`, are UC3's (@sec-a-uc03); `ReviewCase` is added because A5, A12 and A13 set a payment aside for an operator. `attemptKey` is an external key chosen by the browser, not a reference to another entity.

#afig("a-pay-ac", float: true, [Pay upfront analysis class diagram (UML class notation, BCE stereotypes). The Buyer uses `PaymentUI` and Stripe uses `PaymentGateway`. `PayUpfrontControl` alone reaches both boundaries and the entities; it reaches the base use case only through `paymentConfirmed` on the abstract `BaseUseCaseControl` (italic), realised by `StartTeamControl` and `JoinTeamControl`.])

