@fig-a-pay-as-settle draws Stripe's side, B5–B9, with every significant alternate that money depends on: a report that is not genuine (A9), a report already recorded (A11), a page that does not match (A12, A13), a page closed unpaid (A7), and a refund owed because the terms lapsed or the base use case refused (A14, A15). A1, A2, A5, A6, A10, E1 and E2 need design concepts (a feature switch, a rate counter, a provider timeout, a transaction) and appear only in the design sequences. @fig-a-pay-as-prepare draws the buyer's side: preparing the payment (B1–B4, with A3 and A4) and reading the receipt (B10, A8).

