=== Design Class Diagrams <sec-a-pay-dc>

The design is drawn in four slices, all in commerce-svc: capabilities and receipt with the representative persistence chain (@fig-a-pay-dc-receipt), checkout preparation (@fig-a-pay-dc-prepare), the settlement in the payment module (@fig-a-pay-dc-settle) and the webhook entry with Stripe behind its port (@fig-a-pay-dc-gateway). A class shared by two slices shows only the members that slice uses; an operation that two slices use is drawn once, in the first slice that uses it (the settlement slice relies on `findById`, `lock`, `save`, `review` and `now` from @fig-a-pay-dc-prepare). An association means a field reference; a dependency means a parameter, a return value or a created object. A record's component is shown as an attribute, which stands for the association. `ApplicationEventPublisher` is Spring's interface, drawn because the domain event leaves the service through it.

